{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirTableau","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.invSet_garnirPerm_subset_of_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.invSet_garnirPerm_subset_of_descent","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirDescentAdditive.lean#L154-L218","doc":"**Length additivity holds at every descent node.**\n\nFor a row-standard `t` and *any* descent node `(i,j)`, every inversion of the\nGarnir permutation is an inversion of `d(t)` — which by\n`length_dOf_smul_eq_add_iff` is exactly `ℓ(d(t)) = ℓ(d(g_{ij})) + ℓ(w)`.\n\nNo minimality hypothesis: the argument never compares `(i,j)` with any other\ndescent node. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.le_of_col_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.le_of_col_le","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirDescentAdditive.lean#L139-L150","doc":"Along a row, later column means larger label. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.dOf_apply_rowPrefix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.dOf_apply_rowPrefix","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirDescentAdditive.lean#L129-L135","doc":"`dOf t` reads off `t`'s label in the cell that carries the given reference\nlabel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.refTab_apply_rowPrefix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.refTab_apply_rowPrefix","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirDescentAdditive.lean#L117-L127","doc":"The inverse of `refTab_symm_apply`: the label `rowPrefix μ i + c` sits in cell\n`(i, c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.mem_invSet_intervalRotate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GarnirDescentAdditive.mem_invSet_intervalRotate","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GarnirDescentAdditive.lean#L62-L113","doc":"**The inversions of an interval rotation are exactly the \"unwrapped × wrapped\"\npairs.**  With block `[a, a+m)` and shift `k < m`, a pair is inverted only if the\nsmaller entry lies in the part that does not wrap and the larger in the part that\ndoes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}